       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the labeled maximum daily dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some in-range options:\n- **Immediate-release, 850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **Immediate-release, 1,000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Another dose you intended.** For example, 1,700 mg may have been meant as the total daily dose, or the entry may have been a typo.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm the formulation, and I'll enter it right away."
